  "ground_truth": {
    "answer": "Container.securityContext is a SecurityContext object. To add or drop Linux capabilities, use the capabilities field (a Capabilities object) with: add (list of Capability strings to grant, e.g. NET_ADMIN, SYS_TIME) and drop (list of Capability strings to remove, e.g. ALL). Other key SecurityContext fields: runAsUser (integer UID the container process runs as), runAsNonRoot (boolean — reject containers running as UID 0), readOnlyRootFilesystem (boolean — mount the container root filesystem as read-only), allowPrivilegeEscalation (boolean — controls whether the process can gain more privileges than its parent process).",
    "context": [
      "io.k8s.api.core.v1.Container: securityContext field is a SecurityContext object defining per-container security settings",
      "io.k8s.api.core.v1.SecurityContext: capabilities (Capabilities), runAsUser, runAsNonRoot, readOnlyRootFilesystem, and allowPrivilegeEscalation fields control container-level security",
      "io.k8s.api.core.v1.Capabilities: add and drop fields are lists of Capability strings specifying Linux capabilities to grant or remove"
    ],
